From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 21:49:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sys/xattr.h: keep the kernel's XATTR_CREATE out of glibc's
 enum

We include <linux/xattr.h> first so struct xattr_args is defined. That
header also defines XATTR_CREATE and XATTR_REPLACE as macros, and glibc only
learned to notice (via __USE_KERNEL_XATTR_DEFS) and skip its own enum
declaration of the same names in 2.21. On anything older the macros get
substituted into the enum, which does not compile:

  sys/xattr.h:31:3: error: expected identifier before numeric constant

Undefine them before chaining and let glibc declare them again -- to the
very same values.
---
 src/include/override/sys/xattr.h | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/include/override/sys/xattr.h b/src/include/override/sys/xattr.h
index 8823548..f060396 100644
--- a/src/include/override/sys/xattr.h
+++ b/src/include/override/sys/xattr.h
@@ -5,6 +5,18 @@
  * included before the glibc header, otherwise the struct will not be defined. */
 #include <linux/xattr.h>        /* IWYU pragma: export */
 
+/* glibc only learned to skip its own XATTR_CREATE/XATTR_REPLACE enum when the kernel header got
+ * there first (__USE_KERNEL_XATTR_DEFS) in 2.21. On older glibc the macros defined by the include
+ * above get substituted into that enum declaration, which does not compile. Drop them and let
+ * glibc define them again -- to the very same values. */
+#include <features.h>
+#if defined __GLIBC__
+#  if !__GLIBC_PREREQ(2, 21)
+#    undef XATTR_CREATE
+#    undef XATTR_REPLACE
+#  endif
+#endif
+
 #include_next <sys/xattr.h>     /* IWYU pragma: export */
 
 /* Supported since kernel v6.13 (6140be90ec70c39fa844741ca3cc807dd0866394). */
